From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libwifi: make bSTA-MLD status survive mt76 per-link gaps

iface_mlsta_interface_info() returned an error whenever the per-link query
failed, and its final "return ret" leaked the return value of the last inner
loop iteration. Either way wl_mldsta_status() turned it into
UBUS_STATUS_UNKNOWN_ERROR:

  ubus call wifi.bstamld.sta-mld-3 status -> "Unknown error"
  map-agent                              -> bstamld_parse() never gets data
  map-agent                              -> a->bstamld stays empty
  map-agent                              -> wifi_mod_bridge(add) never called
  sta-mld-3                              -> never joins br-lan, no data path
  map-agent                              -> endless "bsta_scan sta-mld-3"

The MLO backhaul itself is fully up the whole time: both links associated and
authorized, EHT rates on 320 MHz. Only the reporting path is dead -- the same
failure mode patch 931 described for AP-MLD, and the same endless bsta_scan
patch 900 fixed for the non-MLD bSTA path.

Three changes, all following the precedent already set in this tree:

1. Tolerate a failing nlwifi_get_mlo_links(): keep the MLD data
   nlwifi_mlsta_interface_info() already returned instead of discarding the
   whole reply (same tolerance patch 936 added to iface_get_mlsta_info).

2. Drop supplicant_sta_info() and radio_get_band_maxrate() from the per-link
   enrichment. Patch 900 removed both from iface_sta_info() because they hang
   on an mt76 bSTA (~25s and ~10s, wchan=do_select) and stall wifi.bsta status
   past map-agent timeout; the MLD path kept calling them. The per-link data
   map-agent needs (macaddr/channel/bandwidth/band/is4addr) comes from nl80211
   and is already copied above.

3. Return 0 on success instead of whatever the last loop iteration left in ret
   -- a link whose ctrl-interface lookup failed made the whole call fail even
   with mlsta fully populated.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c
+++ b/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c
@@ -2039,17 +2039,23 @@
 
 	/* MLO bsta - get all links */
 	ret = nlwifi_get_mlo_links(ifname, BAND_ANY, link, &num);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+	if (ret) {
+		/* mt76: the per-link query can fail for a bSTA MLD even though
+		 * nlwifi_mlsta_interface_info() above already returned the MLD
+		 * macaddr and num_link. Discarding the whole reply here left
+		 * map-agent believing a fully connected bSTA MLD was down.
+		 * Keep what we have and skip only the enrichment. */
+		libwifi_dbg("[%s] %s: get_mlo_links failed, keeping MLD data\n",
+			    ifname, __func__);
+		num = 0;
+	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < mlsta->num_link; i++) {
 		struct wifi_sta *sta;
 
 		sta = &mlsta->sta[i];
 		for (j = 0; j < num; j++) {
-			unsigned long maxrate = 0;
 			struct wifi_mlo_link *l;
-			char *ctrl_iface = NULL;
 
 			l = &link[j];
 
@@ -2061,21 +2067,10 @@
 			sta->bandwidth = l->bandwidth;
 			sta->band = l->band;
 			sta->is4addr = l->is4addr;
-
-			ret = wifi_get_ctrl_interface_band(ifname, sta->band, &ctrl_iface);
-			if (ret)
-				continue;
-
-			ret = supplicant_sta_info(ctrl_iface, sta);
-
-			radio_get_band_maxrate(ifname, sta->band, &maxrate);
-			sta->maxrate = maxrate;
-
-			free(ctrl_iface);
 		}
 	}
 
-	return ret;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int iface_sta_get_stats(const char *ifname, struct wifi_sta_stats *s)
